  "body": "**Audit of one implication in open PR #1779. No new \u03ba; the selected record is unchanged.**\n\nPR #1779 (1337isnot1337, head `1e3128bf`) counts 8 rank-16 diagonal batches of rank-1 climbs in the selected gauge44 provider. That gives +1.72% on the zero-charge ceiling, below the `complex-rank-shape-decoder` 5% gate. The count uses only contiguous runs: any computational event breaks a run, and chunks are 16-aligned.\n\nThat restriction, not the provider, makes the count small. A rank-1 climb on `L r` touches only `L r`, so inside its phase it can move past events that do not touch `L r`. Allowing only that move gives:\n\n- **134 disjoint 16-batches on distinct destinations per orientation** (earliest-deadline greedy; 2,144 of 2,412 rank-1 climbs). The per-phase cap is 149; by phase A 58/58, B 52/67, cleanup_tail 4/4, final 20/20.\n- The retained independent local checker (`research/complex-571-cold14-k492b/code/hpe_audit_local.py`, unchanged; literal scalar/frame/wrapper replay with 25 mutation controls) **accepts the reordered programs**. Their receipt equals the original's, which equals the pinned selected `INDEPENDENT-LOCAL-REPLAY.json`. Two added mutations are rejected: a climb moved past a scalar on its own register, and a climb moved into the next phase.\n- PR #1779's own contiguous rule, re-implemented, counts 8 on the original programs and 134 on the reordered ones.\n- Exact ceilings (`ceiling.py`, grid 10\u207b\u00b9\u2075, #1779's mass-preserving zero-charge convention): 22 batches miss the gate (+4.87%), **23 pass** (+5.11%), and 134 give `a < 0.002358018698467` (+39.5%).\n- Sharp charge headroom at 134 batches under discussion 1596's idle-displacing convention: 1,258 extra rank-1 children per call pass the gate and 1,259 fail (about 9.4 per batch).\n\n**What this changes.** The selected chronology does not close the diagonal-batch route below the gate. The route is decided by the charge #1779 waived: gathering 16 registers at *different* frames into one diagonal rank-16 child, plus copies, frames, hosting, storage, precision and dirty restoration. This package inherits #1779's diagonal-child premise and does not examine it. Batch counts are a greedy lower bound. The bit supplier binds well before +39% (#1605).\n\n**Task card.** Chooser seed `e37fae49558c99b32d319ec695f4f266`, track complex-mechanisms, card `complex-rank-shape-decoder`, scope refined to an audit of #1779 (reason in TASK.json). Base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`. Same archive and member pins as #1779. Claim and finding: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1596#discussioncomment-18921783\n\n**Reproduce**\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/diagonal-batch-commutation/verify.py      # ~12 s, PASS_DIAGONAL_BATCH_COMMUTATION\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/diagonal-batch-commutation\n```\n\nChecked on Python 3.10 and 3.12. The package check and replay pass, and `test_research_*.py` passes (42 tests). This is a finite certificate on the pinned programs, not a construction. Not checked: the physical contract of a diagonal rank-16 child, any gathering/restoration charge, whether global hosting and the idle-remainder frame audit (which use helper busy windows) are insensitive to positions inside a phase (only local replay was re-run), the on-top charge convention, the exact phase-B maximum, full selected cold replay, and independent review.\n\n**Open next questions** (in the README): what a diagonal rank-16 child of frame climbs at different frames costs, set against the 1,258-unit headroom; the on-top convention headroom; and the exact phase-B maximum (52\u201367).\n\n**Credit:** 1337isnot1337 (#1779, diagonal batching premise and contiguous count); Arham Tahir (#1605 / discussion 1596, rank-shape budgets); Douglas Colkitt (#1240 packing ceiling); PR1012 (coverage law); the icekylinx / PR514 / PR433 local-checker lineage; the selected construction lineage.\n\nAI assistance: prepared for Josie Elliston by Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5) in one donated session, with no independent review.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
